*1 [[Shachiko]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Rel]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage instantly tries to overwhelm you immediately with Le'Prude accompanied by various Relic Doges, so use [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] to kill initial few peons, then stall Le'Prude as close to the enemy base as you can manage. Keep at this while using Royal Guards, [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cats]], as well as other rushers like [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]] to quickly take care of the Relic Doges. Eventually, a Sir Rel will spawn, which indicates Shachiko's arrival. Kill him, then lure Shachiko to the [[Cat Base]] and annihilate it with two clean [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] hits, at which point there's basically nothing preventing you from swarming Le'Prude with [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] tanks like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] and [[Master of Selection Darvin (Special Cat)|Master of Selection Darvin]].

If you bring the [[Seasons of Love (Combo)|Seasons of Love]] Combo, the [[Three Kings (Combo)|Three Kings]] Combo and a Rich Cat, a team of maxed [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]], [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Dark Lazer]], and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] can actually kill Le’Prude before Sir Rel even shows up, as the only threatening enemies are Red too. How sad.

==Trivia==
*Merry-Go-Roundcake's Japanese name, Baumu Kaiten Mokuba (バウム回転木馬, "Baum Merry-Go-Round"), is a reference to [[wikipedia:Baumkuchen|baumkuchen]], a kind of German spit cake popular in Japan. This sweet's name translates to "tree cake", as the rings that can be seen in its slices resemble a tree's [[wikipedia:Dendrochronology#Growth rings|growth rings]].

